<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Forming and solving a compound inequality for a greenhouse temperature range</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>{@fname@}, a farmer in {@place@}, needs to keep the indoor temperature (\(T\)) of a greenhouse such that it is strictly greater than <b>\({@L@}^\circ\text{C}\)</b> and less than or equal to <b>\({@U@}^\circ\text{C}\)</b>.</p>

<p>An automatic heater in the greenhouse always adds exactly <b>\({@H@}^\circ\text{C}\)</b> to the current outdoor temperature (\(t\)). Therefore, we can say \(T = t + {@H@}\).</p>

<p>By substituting \(T\) into the compound inequality, determine the range of outdoor temperatures (\(t\)) that will keep the greenhouse in the ideal condition.</p>
<p><i>(Enter the lower and upper bounds of \(t\) in the boxes below.)</i></p>

<p>[[input:ans1]] \( < t \le \) [[input:ans2]]</p>

<div><b>Lower bound:</b> [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div><b>Upper bound:</b> [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>First, we translate the initial temperature constraints into a single compound inequality. The indoor temperature \(T\) must be greater than \({@L@}\) and less than or equal to \({@U@}\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle {@L@} < T \le {@U@} \)
</p>

<p>Next, we substitute the expression for the indoor temperature (\(T = t + {@H@}\)) into the middle of the inequality:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle {@L@} < t + {@H@} \le {@U@} \)
</p>

<p>To isolate the outdoor temperature \(t\), we subtract the heater's contribution (\({@H@}\)) from all three parts of the inequality:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
{@L@} - {@H@} &< t \le {@U@} - {@H@} \\
{@ta1@} &< t \le {@ta2@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>

<p>Hence, the required range for the outdoor temperature is:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \boxed{{@ta1@} < t \le {@ta2@}} \)
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
